1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,131
Two is less than five.

2
00:00:02,131 --> 00:00:03,323
Everyone agrees.

3
00:00:03,723 --> 00:00:05,726
Now put a minus sign on both.

4
00:00:05,726 --> 00:00:07,965
Is minus two less than minus five?

5
00:00:08,415 --> 00:00:10,623
Diya checked the kitchen
freezer to find out.

6
00:00:10,973 --> 00:00:13,726
Minus five degrees is
colder than minus two.

7
00:00:13,726 --> 00:00:15,906
So minus five is the smaller one.

8
00:00:15,906 --> 00:00:17,456
The arrow had to flip!

9
00:00:17,956 --> 00:00:20,959
Why does a minus sign
turn an inequality around?

10
00:00:20,959 --> 00:00:22,662
And how do we solve one?

11
00:00:22,662 --> 00:00:23,876
Let us find out.

12
00:00:24,526 --> 00:00:29,583
To solve an inequality means to find
every value of x that keeps it true.

13
00:00:29,933 --> 00:00:32,628
We use the same moves as for an equation.

14
00:00:32,628 --> 00:00:33,947
With one new rule.

15
00:00:34,447 --> 00:00:35,347
Rule one.

16
00:00:35,221 --> 00:00:38,242
Add or take away the same
number on both sides.

17
00:00:38,242 --> 00:00:39,403
The arrow stays.

18
00:00:39,803 --> 00:00:42,095
Think of two friends on a staircase.

19
00:00:42,095 --> 00:00:43,616
Both climb three steps.

20
00:00:43,616 --> 00:00:45,527
The one below is still below.

21
00:00:45,927 --> 00:00:47,677
Seven is less than ten.

22
00:00:47,677 --> 00:00:49,531
Take away four from both.

23
00:00:49,531 --> 00:00:51,281
Three is less than six.

24
00:00:51,281 --> 00:00:52,229
Still true.

25
00:00:52,829 --> 00:00:53,729
Rule two.

26
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:57,564
Multiply or divide both sides
by the same positive number.

27
00:00:57,564 --> 00:00:58,838
The arrow stays.

28
00:00:59,238 --> 00:01:00,138
Double both.

29
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:02,719
Two less than five becomes
four less than ten.

30
00:01:02,719 --> 00:01:03,910
The order is safe.

31
00:01:04,510 --> 00:01:05,833
Now the surprise.

32
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:08,169
Multiply both sides by minus one.

33
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:10,195
Watch the number line.

34
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:13,826
We slide the multiplier
from one, down to minus one.

35
00:01:14,226 --> 00:01:19,031
Two and five squeeze closer, meet at
zero, then come out on the other side.

36
00:01:19,431 --> 00:01:21,136
Two lands on minus two.

37
00:01:21,136 --> 00:01:22,942
Five lands on minus five.

38
00:01:22,942 --> 00:01:24,598
Five was on the right.

39
00:01:24,598 --> 00:01:26,313
Now it is on the left.

40
00:01:26,713 --> 00:01:30,294
The order turned around, so
the arrow turns around too.

41
00:01:30,294 --> 00:01:32,732
Minus two is greater than minus five.

42
00:01:33,382 --> 00:01:35,423
That is rule two, part two.

43
00:01:35,423 --> 00:01:39,652
When you multiply or divide by a
negative number, flip the sign.

44
00:01:40,402 --> 00:01:41,485
Side by side.

45
00:01:41,485 --> 00:01:43,088
Six is less than ten.

46
00:01:43,088 --> 00:01:45,765
Divide both by two, a positive number.

47
00:01:45,765 --> 00:01:47,519
Three is less than five.

48
00:01:47,519 --> 00:01:48,751
The arrow stays.

49
00:01:49,151 --> 00:01:51,368
Now divide both by minus two.

50
00:01:51,368 --> 00:01:53,413
Minus three and minus five.

51
00:01:53,413 --> 00:01:55,178
Minus three is greater.

52
00:01:55,178 --> 00:01:56,502
The arrow flips.

53
00:01:57,102 --> 00:01:58,002
Your turn.

54
00:01:57,991 --> 00:02:00,569
Minus three x is greater than twelve.

55
00:02:00,569 --> 00:02:02,195
Divide by minus three.

56
00:02:02,195 --> 00:02:05,990
Is x greater than minus four,
or less than minus four?

57
00:02:05,990 --> 00:02:07,300
Pause and decide.

58
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,170
Less than minus four!

59
00:02:12,170 --> 00:02:16,021
We divided by a negative
number, so the arrow flips.

60
00:02:16,021 --> 00:02:18,028
Check x equals minus five.

61
00:02:18,028 --> 00:02:20,924
Minus three times minus five is fifteen.

62
00:02:20,924 --> 00:02:23,202
Fifteen is greater than twelve.

63
00:02:23,202 --> 00:02:24,102
True.

64
00:02:24,459 --> 00:02:25,596
Remember this.

65
00:02:25,596 --> 00:02:29,963
Add, take away, or use a
positive number: the arrow stays.

66
00:02:29,963 --> 00:02:33,565
Multiply or divide by a
negative: the arrow flips.

67
00:02:34,265 --> 00:02:36,823
Now let us solve one, step by step.

68
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:40,105
Four x plus three is less
than six x plus seven.

69
00:02:40,455 --> 00:02:41,355
Step one.

70
00:02:41,262 --> 00:02:43,493
Take away six x from both sides.

71
00:02:43,493 --> 00:02:46,335
Minus two x plus three is less than seven.

72
00:02:47,085 --> 00:02:47,985
Step two.

73
00:02:47,856 --> 00:02:49,934
Take away three from both sides.

74
00:02:49,934 --> 00:02:51,974
Minus two x is less than four.

75
00:02:52,724 --> 00:02:53,624
Step three.

76
00:02:53,614 --> 00:02:55,056
Divide by minus two.

77
00:02:55,056 --> 00:02:57,592
That is negative, so the arrow flips.

78
00:02:57,592 --> 00:02:59,537
x is greater than minus two.

79
00:03:00,287 --> 00:03:01,187
Step four.

80
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:02,050
Draw it.

81
00:03:01,914 --> 00:03:05,950
An empty circle at minus two,
and every number to its right.

82
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:07,828
Check one value.

83
00:03:07,828 --> 00:03:10,423
x equals zero gives three less than seven.

84
00:03:10,423 --> 00:03:11,323
True.

85
00:03:10,937 --> 00:03:12,303
So the answer holds.

86
00:03:12,903 --> 00:03:14,406
Now, a worked example.

87
00:03:14,406 --> 00:03:16,879
It is question ten of the NCERT exercise.

88
00:03:17,229 --> 00:03:21,573
Solve x over three is greater
than x over two, plus one.

89
00:03:22,073 --> 00:03:22,973
Step one.

90
00:03:22,922 --> 00:03:24,401
Fractions are messy.

91
00:03:24,401 --> 00:03:27,639
Multiply both sides by
six, a positive number.

92
00:03:27,639 --> 00:03:30,473
Two x is greater than three x plus six.

93
00:03:31,223 --> 00:03:32,123
Step two.

94
00:03:32,041 --> 00:03:33,428
Take away three x.

95
00:03:33,428 --> 00:03:35,434
Minus x is greater than six.

96
00:03:36,184 --> 00:03:37,084
Step three.

97
00:03:37,067 --> 00:03:38,595
Multiply by minus one.

98
00:03:38,595 --> 00:03:39,495
Flip!

99
00:03:39,133 --> 00:03:40,920
x is less than minus six.

100
00:03:41,670 --> 00:03:45,336
So the answer is every real
number less than minus six.

101
00:03:45,336 --> 00:03:46,668
Test minus twelve.

102
00:03:46,668 --> 00:03:49,242
Minus four is greater than minus five.

103
00:03:49,242 --> 00:03:50,142
True.

104
00:03:50,453 --> 00:03:51,915
Now, the exam trap.

105
00:03:52,265 --> 00:03:54,386
Three x is greater than minus six.

106
00:03:54,386 --> 00:03:56,919
Many students see the minus sign and flip.

107
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:59,183
They write x is less than minus two.

108
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:02,294
But we divide by three, which is positive.

109
00:04:02,294 --> 00:04:04,681
The minus on the six does not matter.

110
00:04:04,681 --> 00:04:08,446
Only the sign of the number you
multiply or divide by decides.

111
00:04:08,446 --> 00:04:10,305
x is greater than minus two.

112
00:04:10,955 --> 00:04:12,417
Where is this asked?

113
00:04:12,417 --> 00:04:16,969
We found no past paper question on
just this step, so no chip lights.

114
00:04:16,969 --> 00:04:21,521
The type: solve and pick the right
interval, often as one step inside a

115
00:04:21,521 --> 00:04:22,619
bigger problem.

116
00:04:23,219 --> 00:04:24,119
Exam level now.

117
00:04:24,109 --> 00:04:26,347
How many integers make
both inequalities true?

118
00:04:26,347 --> 00:04:27,274
Pause and solve.

119
00:04:32,674 --> 00:04:34,081
The answer is C.

120
00:04:34,081 --> 00:04:34,981
Eight.

121
00:04:35,246 --> 00:04:36,146
First one.

122
00:04:36,116 --> 00:04:38,018
Bring the x terms together.

123
00:04:38,018 --> 00:04:40,029
Fifteen is at least three x.

124
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:41,691
So x is at most five.

125
00:04:42,191 --> 00:04:43,091
Second one.

126
00:04:43,089 --> 00:04:44,241
Take away four.

127
00:04:44,241 --> 00:04:46,457
Minus three x is less than nine.

128
00:04:46,457 --> 00:04:48,712
Divide by minus three, and flip.

129
00:04:48,712 --> 00:04:50,772
x is greater than minus three.

130
00:04:51,272 --> 00:04:52,276
Both together.

131
00:04:52,276 --> 00:04:55,422
x is greater than minus
three, and at most five.

132
00:04:55,422 --> 00:04:57,413
That is minus two up to five.

133
00:04:57,413 --> 00:04:58,464
Eight integers.

134
00:04:59,064 --> 00:05:00,605
Here is your recap.

135
00:05:00,605 --> 00:05:02,189
Screenshot this card.

136
00:05:05,389 --> 00:05:07,575
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

137
00:05:07,975 --> 00:05:08,875
One.

138
00:05:08,421 --> 00:05:10,714
Which two moves never change the arrow?

139
00:05:11,614 --> 00:05:12,514
Two.

140
00:05:12,105 --> 00:05:14,291
Solve minus x is less than four.

141
00:05:15,191 --> 00:05:16,091
Three.

142
00:05:15,751 --> 00:05:19,725
Why does multiplying by minus one
flip the order on a number line?

143
00:05:20,825 --> 00:05:23,992
Next time: a straight line
splits a whole field in two.

144
00:05:23,992 --> 00:05:25,028
Which side wins?

145
00:05:25,028 --> 00:05:28,144
We find out with graphs of
inequalities in two variables.
